"use strict";(self.webpackChunksmart_barcode_scan_and_ordering_doc=self.webpackChunksmart_barcode_scan_and_ordering_doc||[]).push([[502],{8179(e,t,r){r.r(t),r.d(t,{_pageData:()=>s,default:()=>n});var a=r(641);const s=JSON.parse('{"path":"/smart-barcode-scan/customer-details.html","title":"Customer Details","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{"title":"Customer Details","description":"Attach an existing WordPress user to a counter order, or register a new customer from inside the Smart Barcode Scan order builder."},"git":{},"filePathRelative":"smart-barcode-scan/customer-details.md"}'),o={name:"customer-details.md"},n=(0,r(6262).A)(o,[["render",function(e,t,r,s,o,n){const i=(0,a.g2)("RouteLink");return(0,a.uX)(),(0,a.CE)("div",null,[t[4]||(t[4]=(0,a.Fv)('<h1 id="customer-details" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#customer-details"><span>Customer Details</span></a></h1><p>An order created from the console can be a guest order or be linked to a user account. Linking it means the customer sees the order in <strong>My account → Orders</strong>, and their purchase history and lifetime value stay accurate.</p><p>The Customer section sits at the top of the <strong>Create Order</strong> sidebar.</p><h2 id="attaching-an-existing-customer" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#attaching-an-existing-customer"><span>Attaching an existing customer</span></a></h2><ol><li>Open the <strong>Create Order</strong> tab.</li><li>Type into <strong>Link order to user</strong>. Searching starts from the first character.</li><li>Pick the right account from the dropdown.</li></ol><p><img src="/smart-barcode-scan-and-ordering/images/smart-barcode-scan/smart-barcode-create-order-customer.png" alt="Searching for a customer by name"></p><p>The search matches on the account <strong>username</strong>, its <strong>URL name</strong> and its <strong>email address</strong>. If nothing matches, it falls back to searching the customer&#39;s <strong>first name</strong> and <strong>last name</strong>. Up to 15 accounts are listed.</p><p>Each result is shown as <code>Display name (#user ID – email address)</code>, so two people with the same name are still easy to tell apart.</p><h3 id="what-happens-when-you-select-someone" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#what-happens-when-you-select-someone"><span>What happens when you select someone</span></a></h3><p>The account is attached to the order and the sidebar fills in from their saved WooCommerce customer profile:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Section</th><th>Filled from the customer&#39;s saved details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Billing</strong></td><td>Address, city, state, postcode, country, phone, email</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Shipping</strong></td><td>Address, city, state, postcode, country, phone; email is set to their account email</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Anything the customer has not saved is left blank for you to complete. Anything already saved can be overwritten for this order without changing their stored profile.</p><h3 id="detaching-a-customer" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#detaching-a-customer"><span>Detaching a customer</span></a></h3><p>Click the <strong>✕</strong> beside the selected customer. The order becomes a guest order; the address fields keep whatever is currently in them, so clear or replace them if they belonged to the previous customer.</p><div class="hint-container tip"><p class="hint-container-title">Tips</p><p>A guest order is perfectly valid. Fill in at least a billing email if you want WooCommerce to be able to email the customer about it.</p></div><h2 id="registering-a-new-customer" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#registering-a-new-customer"><span>Registering a new customer</span></a></h2><p>If the person in front of you has no account, you can create one without leaving the order screen.</p><ol><li>Click <strong>NEW USER</strong> in the sidebar.</li><li>Fill in the form.</li><li>Click <strong>Add New User</strong>.</li></ol><p><img src="/smart-barcode-scan-and-ordering/images/smart-barcode-scan/smart-barcode-create-order-new-user.png" alt="The Add New User form"></p><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Required</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Username</strong></td><td>Yes</td><td>Must not already exist</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Email</strong></td><td>Yes</td><td>Must be a valid address that is not already registered</td></tr><tr><td><strong>First Name</strong></td><td>No</td><td>Also saved as the billing and shipping first name</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Last Name</strong></td><td>No</td><td>Also saved as the billing and shipping last name</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Website</strong></td><td>No</td><td>Saved on the WordPress profile</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Password</strong></td><td>No</td><td>Leave blank and a strong password is generated automatically</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Send the new user an email about their account</strong></td><td>—</td><td>Ticked by default; sends the standard WordPress new-account email</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Role</strong></td><td>—</td><td>Defaults to <strong>Customer</strong>; every role on your site is available</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The new account is created with the details you entered, its WooCommerce billing name, billing email and shipping name are filled in, and it is attached to the order immediately.</p><p>Click <strong>Cancel</strong> to go back to the cart without creating anyone.</p><h3 id="validation-messages" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#validation-messages"><span>Validation messages</span></a></h3><table><thead><tr><th>Message</th><th>Cause</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><em>Username is required.</em></td><td>The Username field was left empty</td></tr><tr><td><em>This username is already registered. Please choose another one.</em></td><td>That username is taken</td></tr><tr><td><em>Valid email is required.</em></td><td>The email is missing or malformed</td></tr><tr><td><em>An account is already registered with your email address.</em></td><td>That email already belongs to an account — search for it instead</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="hint-container important"><p class="hint-container-title">Important</p><p>The <strong>Role</strong> dropdown lists every role on your site, including Administrator. Leave it on <strong>Customer</strong> unless you have a specific reason not to: a counter sale should never create an account with elevated permissions.</p></div><div class="hint-container note"><p class="hint-container-title">Note</p><p>The account-created email is sent by WordPress. If your site cannot send mail, the account is still created correctly — only the notification fails. Give the customer their password another way, or ask them to use the &quot;Lost your password?&quot; link.</p></div><h2 id="how-the-customer-appears-on-the-order" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#how-the-customer-appears-on-the-order"><span>How the customer appears on the order</span></a></h2><p>Once the order is created:</p><ul><li>The WooCommerce order editor shows the linked account in its <strong>Customer</strong> field.</li><li>The order appears under <strong>WooCommerce → Customers</strong> against that account.</li><li>Scanning the order later shows the account&#39;s email in the <strong>Customer</strong> and <strong>User</strong> fields of the Orders tab.</li><li>For a guest order, the console shows the billing email instead, or <em>Guest</em> when there is none.</li></ul><h2 id="next-step" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#next-step"><span>Next step</span></a></h2>',30)),(0,a.Lk)("ul",null,[(0,a.Lk)("li",null,[(0,a.bF)(i,{to:"/smart-barcode-scan/billing-and-shipping.html"},{default:(0,a.k6)(()=>[...t[0]||(t[0]=[(0,a.eW)("Billing & Shipping",-1)])]),_:1}),t[1]||(t[1]=(0,a.eW)(" — completing the address details.",-1))]),(0,a.Lk)("li",null,[(0,a.bF)(i,{to:"/smart-barcode-scan/create-order.html"},{default:(0,a.k6)(()=>[...t[2]||(t[2]=[(0,a.eW)("Create Order",-1)])]),_:1}),t[3]||(t[3]=(0,a.eW)(" — the rest of the order flow.",-1))])])])}]])}}]);